<%# The permission checkbox grid, shared by the add form and the edit form.

    ONE partial rather than two grids on purpose. The two forms make the same promise — "these are
    the permissions you may hand to this person" — and a grid duplicated per form is how the add
    door and the edit door drift into offering different sets, which on this feature means one of
    them offers a box whose save is then refused.

    `permissions` is the caller's `repository_policy.grantable_permissions`, NOT
    RepositoryMembership::PERMISSIONS. That reader was built for exactly this and says so: "the set
    an 'add/edit member' form should render checkboxes from — so the grid offers only what the save
    will accept, rather than options that are rejected on submit." Rendering the full set instead
    would show a `members.manage` holder a `repo.delete` box that
    `grantor_holds_every_granted_permission` refuses on submit, i.e. a control that can only ever
    422.

    `param_name` differs because the two forms post different objects: the add form posts a
    MembershipGrant (a typed handle is not an attribute of a membership row), the edit form posts
    the RepositoryMembership itself (the row already names its user).
%>
<% permissions.each do |permission| %>
  <label class="flex items-start gap-2 rounded-md border border-app-border-light bg-app-surface-raised p-3">
    <%= check_box_tag "#{param_name}[permissions][]", permission, selected.include?(permission),
                      id: "#{param_name}_permissions_#{permission.parameterize}",
                      class: "mt-0.5 rounded border-app-border-light" %>
    <span class="space-y-0.5">
      <span class="block font-mono text-sm text-app-content"><%= permission %></span>
      <span class="block text-xs text-app-muted"><%= grant_permission_description(permission) %></span>
    </span>
  </label>
<% end %>
